# Overview

This is a production Hotel PMS Admin application.
The agent must operate in a strict, delivery-focused mode.

This rule exists to prevent over-engineering, unwanted files,
and speculative architecture changes.

# Absolute Restrictions

- Do NOT generate or modify any `.md` files (README, docs, notes, CLAUDE.md, etc.).
- Do NOT create new files or folders unless explicitly instructed.
- Do NOT introduce Redux, Zustand, Context API, or any global state library.
- Do NOT add token handling, JWT storage, refresh tokens, or session logic.
- Do NOT add authentication logic on the frontend.
- Do NOT add new dependencies or libraries.
- Do NOT refactor unrelated code.
- Do NOT generate boilerplate, scaffolding, or sample/demo files.

# Frontend Authority Rules

- Backend APIs are the single source of truth.
- Frontend must NEVER calculate:
  - prices
  - GST / tax
  - totals
  - availability
  - discounts
- Frontend only triggers actions and renders responses.

# Coding Constraints

- Modify ONLY the file(s) explicitly mentioned by the user.
- One component must not exceed 250 lines.
- One component = one responsibility.
- Follow existing project patterns exactly.
- No speculative abstractions.
- No premature optimizations.

# Workflow Discipline

- Build ONE page or ONE feature at a time.
- Stop after completing the requested task.
- Do NOT continue to the next step without confirmation.
- If a request is ambiguous, ASK before acting.

# Allowed Behavior

- Explanations are allowed without code.
- Code generation is allowed ONLY when explicitly requested.
- Suggestions must be minimal and directly relevant.

# Failure Mode

If any instruction would violate these rules:
- STOP immediately
- Explain why it violates the rule
- Ask how to proceed
